      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two minor suggestions for the commit message:\n\n1. **`BUG\u003d` footer format:** ChromiumOS commit messages expect a bug tracker reference in `BUG\u003db:\u003cbug_id\u003e` format (or `BUG\u003dnone` if no individual bug exists) rather than `BUG\u003dhotlistid:9083583`.\n2. **Avoid low-level code narration in the body:** The second paragraph (`by returning EC_RES_SUCCESS with 0 response_size`) restates implementation details that are already clear from the diff. Keeping the description focused on the high-level behavior makes it easier to scan:\n\n```text\ncommon/panic_output: suppress SW_WATCHDOG_WARN from AP crash reporter\n\nPANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN is a non-fatal warning generated by the EC that\ndoes not trigger an EC reset. However, the AP reads it via\nEC_CMD_GET_PANIC_INFO and uploads it to UMA as a fatal crash, causing\nZero-CPMH false positive spikes (e.g. 4869 CPMH on kappa).\n\nReturn an empty panic info response when the panic reason is\nPANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN so non-fatal watchdog warnings are not reported\nas crashes to the AP.\n\nBUG\u003db:\u003cbug_id\u003e\nTEST\u003dcros_sdk -- make run-panic_watchdog_warn\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/7213684c-af67-4168-addc-71b274a4624b)",
