      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please address the blocking issues in the inline comments.\n\n### Review Summary\n- **Functionality**: ⚠️ `panic_get_reason(\u0026reason, NULL, NULL)` in `common/panic_output.c` passes `NULL` for `info` and `exception`, which all `core/*/panic.c` implementations unconditionally dereference (`*info` and `*exception`), causing a `NULL` pointer write on every `EC_CMD_GET_PANIC_INFO` call. The call also needs an `#ifdef CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC` guard.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: ✅ Filtering `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN` in `host_command_panic_info` suppresses false-positive AP crash reports while preserving the saved panic data in RAM so `system_common_pre_init()` can still promote it to `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG` if a real watchdog reset follows.\n- **Code Simplicity**: ⚠️ `test/panic_watchdog_warn.c` includes unused headers (`software_panic.h`, `sysjump.h`), unused `mock_memory` fields (`pad`, `jdata`), and an unused `software_panic()` stub.\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: ✅ Follows ChromiumOS EC conventions and naming patterns.\n- **Security**: ⚠️ Passing `NULL` pointers into `panic_get_reason` causes an arbitrary write of `0` to address `0x0` when handling `EC_CMD_GET_PANIC_INFO`.\n- **Testing**: ⚠️ The mock `panic_get_reason` in `test/panic_watchdog_warn.c` added `NULL` checks not present in production `core/*/panic.c` (masking the `NULL` dereference bug), and the test only verifies the suppressed `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN` path without verifying that fatal panic reasons (e.g., `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG`) are still reported.\n- **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: ✅ Focused, self-contained change (+122, -0 lines) pairing the host command fix with a unit test.\n- **Commit Message**: ⚠️ Minor suggestion to use `BUG\u003db:\u003cbug_id\u003e` instead of `BUG\u003dhotlistid:9083583` and avoid low-level return-code narration in the body.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/7213684c-af67-4168-addc-71b274a4624b)",
