      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Calling `panic_get_reason(\u0026reason, NULL, NULL)` unconditionally causes a **`NULL` pointer dereference** on every `EC_CMD_GET_PANIC_INFO` call and breaks builds when `CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC` is disabled:\n\n1. **Unconditional `NULL` pointer dereference:** Every architecture implementation of `panic_get_reason(uint32_t *reason, uint32_t *info, uint8_t *exception)` (`core/cortex-m0/panic.c`, `core/cortex-m/panic.c`, `core/riscv-rv32i/panic.c`, `core/nds32/panic.c`, and `core/minute-ia/panic.c`) unconditionally writes to `*reason`, `*info`, and `*exception` without checking for `NULL`—both when panic data is valid and in the `else` branch (`*exception \u003d *reason \u003d *info \u003d 0;`). Passing `NULL` for `info` and `exception` writes to address `0x0` (`*(uint32_t *)NULL` and `*(uint8_t *)NULL`), which is undefined behavior and either corrupts memory at `0x0` or triggers a hardware fault depending on the target memory map. (Compare `common/system.c:764`, which passes valid local variables `\u0026reason, \u0026info, \u0026exception`. The unit test in `test/panic_watchdog_warn.c` masked this bug because its mock added `if (info)` and `if (exception)` checks that do not exist in `core/*/panic.c`.)\n2. **Missing `#ifdef CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC` guard:** In `include/panic.h:175-192` and `core/*/panic.c`, `panic_get_reason` is only declared and defined when `CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC` is enabled (and this file already guards software-panic usage with `#ifdef CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC` at lines 25, 112, and 124). Calling `panic_get_reason` unconditionally breaks builds where `CONFIG_COMMON_PANIC_OUTPUT` is enabled without `CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC`.\n\nPass valid local variables for `info` and `exception` and guard the check with `#ifdef CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC`:\n\n```c\n#ifdef CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC\n\tuint32_t reason \u003d 0;\n\tuint32_t info;\n\tuint8_t exception;\n\n\tpanic_get_reason(\u0026reason, \u0026info, \u0026exception);\n\n\t/* Do not report watchdog warnings to AP to prevent false CPMH spikes */\n\tif (reason \u003d\u003d PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN)\n\t\treturn EC_RES_SUCCESS;\n#endif\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/7213684c-af67-4168-addc-71b274a4624b)",
