      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two issues in the mock and test scaffolding here:\n\n1. **Mock `panic_get_reason` masks `NULL` pointer dereferences (`lines 50–58`):** Checking `if (reason)`, `if (info)`, and `if (exception)` diverges from all production `core/*/panic.c` implementations, which unconditionally dereference all three pointers. This discrepancy prevented the unit test from catching the `NULL` arguments passed in `common/panic_output.c:382`. Assert `ASSERT(reason \u0026\u0026 info \u0026\u0026 exception)` and dereference all three pointers unconditionally so the mock enforces the production contract.\n2. **Unused headers, struct fields, and stub (`lines 10, 12, 14–25, 39, 60–63`):**\n   - `software_panic()` (`lines 39, 60–63`) is never referenced by `common/panic_output.c` when `CONFIG_DEBUG_ASSERT_REBOOTS` is undefined on line 35, and `#include \"software_panic.h\"` (`line 10`) is already included transitively by `panic.h`.\n   - `pad` and `jdata` in `struct mock_memory` (`lines 14–18`, along with `#include \"sysjump.h\"` on line 12) are only needed by `get_panic_data_write()`, which this test never calls; a single `static struct panic_data mock_pdata` is sufficient.\n\n```c\n#include \"common.h\"\n#include \"host_command.h\"\n#include \"panic.h\"\n#include \"task.h\"\n#include \"test_util.h\"\n\nstatic struct panic_data mock_pdata;\n\n#undef PANIC_DATA_PTR\n#define PANIC_DATA_PTR (\u0026mock_pdata)\n#undef CONFIG_PANIC_DATA_BASE\n#define CONFIG_PANIC_DATA_BASE ((uintptr_t)\u0026mock_pdata)\n\n#undef CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC\n#define CONFIG_SOFTWARE_PANIC\n\n#undef CONFIG_DEBUG_ASSERT_REBOOTS\n#undef CONFIG_CMD_CRASH\n\nvoid panic_get_reason(uint32_t *reason, uint32_t *info, uint8_t *exception);\n\n/* Dummy implementation for panic_data_print */\nvoid panic_data_print(const struct panic_data *pdata)\n{\n}\n\n#include \"../common/panic_output.c\"\n\nstatic uint32_t mock_reason;\n\nvoid panic_get_reason(uint32_t *reason, uint32_t *info, uint8_t *exception)\n{\n\tASSERT(reason \u0026\u0026 info \u0026\u0026 exception);\n\t*reason \u003d mock_reason;\n\t*info \u003d 0;\n\t*exception \u003d 0;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/7213684c-af67-4168-addc-71b274a4624b)",
