      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This test only covers the suppressed `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN` path and includes conditional setup (`if (pdata)`) in the test body:\n\n1. **Missing test coverage for non-suppressed panic reasons:** Because only `mock_reason \u003d PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN` is tested, the test would still pass with `args.response_size \u003d\u003d 0` even if `host_command_panic_info` suppressed all panic reasons or if `pdata` failed validation (`pdata_start \u003d\u003d 0`). Add a companion test verifying that a fatal panic reason—such as `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG` (which `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN` is promoted to on an actual watchdog reset) or adjacent `PANIC_SW_EXIT`—still returns `sizeof(struct panic_data)` bytes and sets `PANIC_DATA_FLAG_OLD_HOSTCMD` on `mock_pdata.flags` (while `PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN` leaves `PANIC_DATA_FLAG_OLD_HOSTCMD` cleared).\n2. **Avoid conditional branching in the test body (`lines 72–75`):** Initialize `mock_pdata` directly rather than guarding setup behind `if (pdata)`.\n\n```c\ntest_static int test_get_panic_info_watchdog_warn(void)\n{\n\tstruct host_cmd_handler_args args \u003d { 0 };\n\tuint8_t response_buf[sizeof(struct panic_data)] \u003d { 0 };\n\n\tmemset(\u0026mock_pdata, 0, sizeof(mock_pdata));\n\tmock_pdata.magic \u003d PANIC_DATA_MAGIC;\n\tmock_pdata.struct_size \u003d sizeof(struct panic_data);\n\tmock_reason \u003d PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG_WARN;\n\n\targs.command \u003d EC_CMD_GET_PANIC_INFO;\n\targs.response \u003d response_buf;\n\targs.response_max \u003d sizeof(response_buf);\n\n\t/* The host command should return SUCCESS with response_size 0 */\n\tTEST_EQ(host_command_process(\u0026args), EC_RES_SUCCESS, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(args.response_size, 0, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_BITS_CLEARED((int)mock_pdata.flags, PANIC_DATA_FLAG_OLD_HOSTCMD);\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n\ntest_static int test_get_panic_info_watchdog_fatal(void)\n{\n\tstruct host_cmd_handler_args args \u003d { 0 };\n\tuint8_t response_buf[sizeof(struct panic_data)] \u003d { 0 };\n\n\tmemset(\u0026mock_pdata, 0, sizeof(mock_pdata));\n\tmock_pdata.magic \u003d PANIC_DATA_MAGIC;\n\tmock_pdata.struct_size \u003d sizeof(struct panic_data);\n\tmock_reason \u003d PANIC_SW_WATCHDOG;\n\n\targs.command \u003d EC_CMD_GET_PANIC_INFO;\n\targs.response \u003d response_buf;\n\targs.response_max \u003d sizeof(response_buf);\n\n\t/* Fatal watchdog panics must still be reported to the AP */\n\tTEST_EQ(host_command_process(\u0026args), EC_RES_SUCCESS, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(args.response_size, sizeof(struct panic_data), \"%d\");\n\tTEST_BITS_SET((int)mock_pdata.flags, PANIC_DATA_FLAG_OLD_HOSTCMD);\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n\nint task_test(void *data)\n{\n\ttest_reset();\n\tRUN_TEST(test_get_panic_info_watchdog_warn);\n\tRUN_TEST(test_get_panic_info_watchdog_fatal);\n\ttest_print_result();\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/7213684c-af67-4168-addc-71b274a4624b)",
